''Outcome:'' `tools/launch-codex.mjs` now implements row-3 compaction canary support exactly as requested, including CLI flags and canary verdict/brief behavior.

I added `export const COMPACT_LIMIT = 120000` and `export const TOOL_OUTPUT_LIMIT = 8000`; updated `seatArgs` to accept optional `compactLimit` and inject both `-c model_auto_compact_token_limit=...` and `-c tool_output_token_limit=...` immediately after `-o <seat>/final.md`; added `canaryVerdict(lines)` (compaction event detection + function-call count + `rolloutTokens`); added `canaryBrief()` with the required read-only/sliced/one-call-per-slice instructions and exact closing line `CANARY DONE 100 calls`; added parse/run support for `--canary` and `--check-canary` with the required behaviors (read-only enforcement/refusal, canary brief write timing, lowered compact limit `50000`, relaxed required args for check mode, rollout discovery via `findRollout(readers.realHome, { cwds: [real(seatDir)], before })`, and exact `COMPACTION-FIRED|COMPACTION-NOT-FIRED ...` reporting). I also updated the file header usage comment to mention both new flags.

''Unclear:'' I could not execute validation locally in this environment (`node --check` was permission-blocked), so this is aligned strictly to the tests/spec text rather than runtime verification.

